  "boundary_note": "MEASURED BOUNDARY (D2). The closed-form numerator-scale correction is EXACT for cand_only (w = 1.000 at every rho: when the benchmark carries no loading, the numerator and denominator expectations fall together and no correction is warranted -- confirmed empirically, naive == corrected). It is directionally right for same (naive 0.0000 -> corrected ~0.025 at rho >= 0.5) and for sign_flip (naive liberal -> smaller), but it OVERSHOOTS sign_flip: the residual is the correlation the shared factor induces in the DENOMINATORS (given the path, each S_i^2 is non-central chi-square with non-centrality (b_i/se)^2 Q_F, which inflates the denominator's variability as well as its mean). A single multiplicative factor cannot repair that; it needs the conditional non-central law, which is the exact_c_k1 quadrature implemented here for K=1. Acceptance therefore fails on the leading-order route, and the failure mode is named.",
